  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Pterygoplichthys etentaculatus (Spix &amp; Agassiz, 1829). Maximum size 30 cm SL. Type locality: Rio São Francisco, Januaria, Minas Gerais State, Brazil. IUCN Red List: Least Concern (last assessed 2018).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>South America: São Francisco River basin. Also recorded from the Rio Carinhanha.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<ul><li>pH: 6.2–7.8</li><li>Temperature: 22–30°C</li><li>Other parameters: dH 25</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Omnivorous and a good algae eater, especially when young.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Suggested tankmates: almost any medium sized community fish.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Comparison of the genital papilla in mature fish shows the differences in the sexes to the trained eye. In males this is a small yet thick stump which noticeably protrudes from the fish's undercarriage. In females it is less obvious and is recessed or lies flat with the body.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Unreported. There is no breeding report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Pterygoplichthys can be identified by the number of rays in the dorsal fin. Ten or more dorsal rays (usually more than 10) indicates that it's a Pterygoplichthys. Most other plecos have 8 or fewer rays (in particular the larger Hypostomus species that are most likely to be confused with Pterygoplichthys).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1348",
      "html": "<p>Selecta genera et species piscium quos in itinere per Brasiliam, pp 7, Pl. 4 (figs. 1-2).</p>"
    }
  ],
